From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathias Fredriksson <mafredri@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:51:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] ICP: AES_GCM: Return generic ops for sse4_1

With icp_gcm_impl=sse4_1, contexts the isalc code can't handle (IV
length other than 12 bytes, or tag length other than 64, 96 or 128 bits)
fall back to the generic GCM path. gcm_impl_get_ops() had no case for
IMPL_SSE4_1, so it returned NULL and the fallback crashed calling
through it. Handle it like IMPL_AVX.

Signed-off-by: Mathias Fredriksson <mafredri@gmail.com>
---
 module/icp/algs/modes/gcm.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/module/icp/algs/modes/gcm.c b/module/icp/algs/modes/gcm.c
index 712bb9bea50a..7aca9b2b57f1 100644
--- a/module/icp/algs/modes/gcm.c
+++ b/module/icp/algs/modes/gcm.c
@@ -1065,11 +1065,15 @@ gcm_impl_get_ops(void)
 		ops = gcm_supp_impl[idx];
 		break;
 #ifdef CAN_USE_GCM_ASM
+#ifdef CAN_USE_GCM_ASM_SSE
+	case IMPL_SSE4_1:
+#endif
 	case IMPL_AVX:
 		/*
 		 * Make sure that we return a valid implementation while
-		 * switching to the avx implementation since there still
-		 * may be unfinished non-avx contexts around.
+		 * switching to a SIMD implementation since there still
+		 * may be unfinished non-SIMD contexts around. Contexts
+		 * the SIMD code can't handle also use these ops.
 		 */
 		ops = &gcm_generic_impl;
 		break;
